From a6a46252aa4f00be821c391f21036bdd6d3ce6bc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Vincent Leon <leon@mbp.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 15:42:30 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] feat: alert devices that take alerts over their connection
 where the daemon would push

The daemon gives an attention alert to the most recently present client,
or pushes when none is present, so a backgrounded Android device that
takes alerts over its connection was never alerted: after three minutes
away every alert became a push, which it does not take.

A client now says so in its heartbeat (alertsOverConnection, optional),
and the daemon marks shouldNotify for such clients exactly when it would
push. A present desktop keeps the alert to itself, as with push. The
daemon advertises server_info.features.alertsOverConnection. Against a
daemon without it, the app alerts whenever it is not in front, tagged
COMPAT for removal once every fork daemon has the feature.

Protocol: both fields are optional. Older daemons ignore the heartbeat
field and older apps the feature flag.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
